# Commit conventions

Canonical git policy: `core/policies/git.md`. Branch and worktree model: `rules/dev/git-worktree-agent-workflow.md`.

## Format

```
<type>(<scope>): <description>
```

**Types:** `feat`, `fix`, `chore`, `docs`, `refactor`
**Scopes:** `skills`, `hooks`, `core`, `rules`, `marketplace`, `ci`, `docs`

```
feat(skills): add pr-dev skill for persistent PR drive loop
fix(hooks): handle missing session state in capture-task-slug
chore(ci): switch ubuntu runner to ubuntu-latest
```

## Branches

```
objective/<slug>        integration branch — where the PR comes from
worker/<slug>/NNN       one worker task
```

## Rules

- One commit per logical change — never batch unrelated fixes
- Never `git add .` — stage specific files, so secrets and build artifacts cannot ride along
- Never push directly to the default branch — branch, then PR
- `make validate` must pass before the objective's PR opens
